# Bits Pay service work

This repo (`bitspay-core`) holds 12 standalone Spring Boot services under `services/<svc>/`. Code is 100 % agent-written from the spec pack.

Before any work on a service:
1. Read `services/<svc>/CLAUDE.md` completely and treat it as binding — it was written for Claude Code but applies to you unchanged. Its paths are relative to `services/<svc>/`.
2. Follow its "Read first" order (SPEC.md, contract.yaml, provided/, consumed/, then `docs/global/GLOBAL-CONVENTIONS.md`).

Always:
- One work package (SPEC §10) per chat. Plan first, implement only after the developer approves.
- Edit only `services/<svc>/`. Never read or import another service's code. The developer runs `make lock svc=<svc>` before the chat; hooks then block edits to other services. Never change or remove `.agent-scope` yourself.
- Never edit `docs/contracts/**`, `contract.yaml`, `codes.yaml` or golden vectors — use `/raise-cr`.
- Run Gradle from `services/<svc>/` (`./gradlew check`); repo checks from the root (`make verify`).
- Never weaken, delete or disable tests to get green; never lower coverage thresholds.
- Never merge. Commit only in `/finish-wp`.

Workflow commands: `/start-wp`, `/implement-wp`, `/review-wp`, `/fix-gate`, `/finish-wp`, `/raise-cr` — see `docs/AI-IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE.md`.
